ed with daily rotation, 7-rotation retention, gzip compression, and copytruncate to allow continued writes, and each of these behaviors was directly demonstrated through repeated forced rotation cycles rather than merely configured. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was also completed cleanly, with a healthy pre-restart baseline, a restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity consistent with the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and full post-restart recovery of crond, the config, and all rotated data. No unnecessary or unreverted mutations were found beyond the retained rotation artifacts, which are the intended output of the task.","limitations":["Rotation was verified via forced (logrotate -f) invocations rather than observing an actual unattended daily cron firing, though this is a standard and accepted way to validate a logrotate configuration's behavior.","Continued-writes behavior was demonstrated by manual test writes rather than by a real, continuously-running inventory application process, since no live inventory service/process was found on the node."]},"ttft_ms":18377,"type":"result","duration_ms":60957,"uuid":"df905924-57e4-4ae5-a5d1-599877000ea1","ttft_stream_ms":2693,"time_to_request_ms":410,"first_content_frame_ms":2693,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
